A||N||12||87PegasusGT||Turbo T3?||||1||
Z||000000||87PegasusGT||01-26-2000||03:49 PM||||I can get a T-3/T-4 turbo from a 81-87 300zx turbo for $400. Should I buy it? Can I use it on my 3.4? How does one go about a twin turbo?||||reg||1
Z||000001||william_thorniii||01-26-2000||06:30 PM||||Unless you are getting the entire set-up (exhaust, intercooler, adjustable wastegate etc.), $400 sounds very high.  A T3 is a Garrett model.  They are the same brand used in early to mid-eighties Chryslers and T-birds.  One can be obtained from a bone yard for around $75-$100.  Usually they need to be rebuilt, but that only doubles your purchase price.  <P>As far as the tt set-up.  Check out this picture!  [img]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Twin Turbo1.jpg[/img]<P>[img]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Twin Turbo1.jpg[/img]<P>William T. Thorn, III<p>[This message has been edited by william_thorniii (edited 01-26-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000002||87PegasusGT||01-26-2000||06:33 PM||||Are they still around?<BR>This will work on a 3.4 right?||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||01-26-2000||06:43 PM||||Pegasus,<P>I must have that problem of getting throught the firewall.  I will try to send them to your e-mail.  No the company is not around any longer.  I hear that they were garbage anyway.  It would work unchanged on a pushrod 3.4 (not the TDC).  I think that it was Stroker who advertised that he would be offering a kit in the near future several months ago and has since disappeared. <P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||10
Z||000004||cobra427||01-26-2000||08:30 PM||||Pegasus, the name of the company was IFG-<BR>International Fiberglass Co. They where around in the early 90's. Still in business <BR>but no longer involved in the T/T .William,<BR>William, isn't garbage a little strong to use? Granted they not of the best design,but <BR>with a little more R/D they could have been a nice package. I have the kit myself and plan on making it a good working system. If you notice that a lot of the newer cars coming out on the market are fitted with the T/T setup. No reason why it can't work on the Fiero.      BTW if you have that site <BR>Will3  I would love for you to share it with me as well. Thanks.<p>[This message has been edited by cobra427 (edited 01-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||01-26-2000||09:57 PM||||Thats what I am using a Garret T3 from a t-bird. I got it for $50 and did the rebuild for another $50||||reg||1
Z||000006||william_thorniii||01-26-2000||10:08 PM||||427,<P>Terribly to offend you.  From what I have heard the system was garbage... Perhaps my information was incorrect and you can help me clear it up.  Was the system ever successfully incorporated on an MPFI engine? As I understand it was designed for the carb'ed S-10 2.8L.  I am not in any way criticising tt set ups... in fact I am a huge advocate of having two different sized turbos (T2 & T3) for our applications.  By doing so, one reduces turbo lag and still has plenty left at the top end.  Again, I am sorry if I offended you.  The simple matter of the fact is that they were not a very good product and certainly were not as good as many others on the market.  I will happily send you the pictures/article but it must be to your personal account as my firewall will not allow me to post pictures.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||6
Z||000007||four50four||01-26-2000||10:37 PM||||i think the reason the pics arn't working is the spaces. when you upload them, try replacing all spaces with "_"<p>[This message has been edited by four50four (edited 01-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||cobra427||01-26-2000||10:58 PM||||will3, this is one of the problems with writting the English language.When written,the sender can try and portray a certain feeling or emotion and sometimes it works, with the aid of commas,exclamation marks, symbols, etc,etc.----And the reader can sometimes look at a post and see it totally different. Its too bad we didn't have all the "charactors" like the Chinese or Japanese. Being that we don't have the aid of our sight, to see the body language,or our ears to hear the voice inflextion,it makes it a little more difficult for the "read". <BR>Now my point.(geesh I thought he'd never get there)Really and truely ,I was not offended.Thats what this forum is all about.Different people likeing different things with a different approaches to their Fieros. I guess I should have used a couple more smile icons huh?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">But don't ever call them garbage again!!!!!   HEY! I'M KIDDING   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Please send to  cobra@c4.net. T/A<p>[This message has been edited by cobra427 (edited 01-26-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000009||WKDFIRO||01-27-2000||02:53 AM||||The answer to your question is yes they will work on the 3.4. We should still have one at the shop on a 3.4 automatic GT with an intercooler. At least I think its a T3. I could be wrong... There are still a lot of things to consider when putting in a turbo. There is a whole lot of planning involved, such as if your injectors will be enough, the ECM needs to be considered, mounting of the turbo and waste gate etc, the strength of the exhaust manifolds, if you are going to modify the manifolds the clearance needed so that you don't fry and melt things....its all way to complicated for my taste but it will work and the results are pretty frighteningly fast.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 01-27-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000010||batboy||01-27-2000||06:24 PM||||I know why people like turbos, but I don't get why it's necessary to use a twin turbo on a Fiero, especially since there is much more expense involved and not really much room in the engine compartment.||||reg||1
Z||000011||87PegasusGT||01-27-2000||06:32 PM||||Batboy: Because its all the difference between 270hp and 340hp. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||william_thorniii||01-27-2000||06:53 PM||||Pegasus,<P>Actually I have completely different reasons for wanting a tt system.  I eventually am going to be building a DOHC tt engine.  My intention for the tt is to have one small charger, probably a T2, and another larger charger, probably a T3.  The smaller charger will spool up much faster since it has a much smaller impeller and therefore a lower mass moment of inertia.  This would significantly reduce the "Turbo lag" that many engines experience. <P>Batboy,<P>Why do I want to go with a turbo setup?  Simple... it is CHEAP.  For the price of a custom bent exhaust you can get into the game.  Of course there are a few other goodies that you need as well, but your basic system can easily be outfitted from the bone yard.  Check out Dennis LaGrua's webpage (forgot the address).  His first 2.8L was put together for well under $1000.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
